            <ArticleTitle>True hermaphroditism presenting as intermittent hematuria and groin pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>133-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>True hermaphroditism was diagnosed when a male was evaluated for inguinal swelling and hematuria. A true hermaphrodite rarely has bilaterally descended gonads. This patient had intrascrotal ovotestes. Diagnosis and management of the true hermaphrodite are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
